[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.85]
\draw[gray!30,very thin,xstep=1,ystep=1] (0,0) grid (6,5);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,5.6);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(6.6,0);
\foreach \v/\p in {10/1,20/2,30/3,40/4,50/5} {\draw (-0.15,\p)--(0,\p); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,\p) {$\v$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4,5,6} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\draw[very thick,blue] (0,1.5)--(6,5.1);
\foreach \pt in {(0,1.5),(6,5.1)} {\fill[blue] \pt circle (2pt);}
\node[rotate=90,font=\scriptsize] at (-1.3,2.5) {Volume in paddling pool (L)};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (3,-1.0) {Time (minutes)};
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (3,5.3) {Filling a paddling pool};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
A paddling pool already has some water in it when a hose starts filling it at a constant rate, as shown. Find the rate at which the pool is filling, in L/min.

