\foreach \x in {2,4,6,8,10} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\draw[very thick,blue] (0,5)--(10,2.5);
\draw[very thick,red] (0,5)--(10,1);
\foreach \pt in {(0,5),(10,2.5),(10,1)} {\fill[black] \pt circle (2pt);}
\node[font=\scriptsize,blue,below left] at (2,4.4) {Candle P};
\node[font=\scriptsize,red,above right] at (6,1.7) {Candle Q};
\node[rotate=90,font=\scriptsize] at (-1.3,2.5) {Height (cm)};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (5,-1.0) {Time (hours)};
\node[font=\scriptsize] at (5,5.3) {Two candles burning};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Two identical candles are lit at the same time and burn down at different constant rates, as shown. Which candle burns faster, and by how much?

